cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Truss in research, engineering documentation, or agent workflows, please cite this repository."
title: "Truss: A Framework for Engineering Trade-offs in Product Systems"
authors:
  - given-names: "Leonardo"
    family-names: "Reis Dias"
version: "0.3.0-research-beta"
date-released: "2026-05-26"
repository-code: "https://github.com/leoreisdias/truss-framework"
url: "https://github.com/leoreisdias/truss-framework"
license: "Apache-2.0 AND CC-BY-4.0"
abstract: "Truss is a research-beta framework for evaluating engineering trade-offs in product systems. It treats software quality as a decision problem organized around Maintainability, Strategy, Clarity, and Performance, with Security handled as a transversal boundary constraint. The repository includes the framework documentation and an evolving LLM/agent skill adapter; field validation and case studies are still in progress."
keywords:
  - engineering trade-offs
  - software quality
  - decision framework
  - maintainability
  - strategy
  - clarity
  - performance
  - LLM agents
